From d4d43841244db7bec62bdb13158f13b5ec01cbe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:10:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] ASoC: qcom: x1e80100: run the speakers at their DT operating
 point

The card keeps the WSA speakers at -3 dB digital gain with the PA at its
floor, about 0.7 V peak on the HP OmniBook Ultra 14, far below what the
speakers take with protection running. The safe operating point is now
in each amplifier's DT node, but it only holds on the gain path it was
measured on, and SP VI must model the same full scale.

When speaker protection is required and every amplifier has an
operating point and the V/I guard, set up that path at late probe,
before userspace can reach a control: each interpolator fed only from
its own AIF1 input, compander and soft clip off, 0 dB digital gain, the
amplifiers in speaker mode at their PA ceiling. These controls are read
back, made read-only and checked at every WSA RX0 prepare, and the full
scale is passed to audioreach. A read-only "Speaker Operating Point
Switch" shows when this is active; otherwise the default limits stay.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
